# {{ .ProjectName }}

Minimal Python 3.13+ project generated by AIAI CLI (python-minimal v1).

## Setup

Install Git, uv, and Node.js 22+ with Corepack available, then run these commands
from this directory. If your Node distribution omits Corepack, install it using
the official Corepack instructions first.

```bash
git init
corepack enable
pnpm install
uv lock
uv sync
```

Commit both `uv.lock` and `pnpm-lock.yaml` before pushing. The CI workflow uses
`uv sync --locked` and deliberately requires the lockfile. AIAI generates files
only; it does not install dependencies, initialize Git, or activate hooks.

The `prepare` script activates Husky during `pnpm install`, after Git is
initialized. Husky uses pnpm/Node only for Git hooks. Python dependencies remain
managed by uv. This project is not configured for package publication.

## Development

```bash
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check .
uv run pyright
uv run pytest
```

Application code lives in `{{ .PackageName }}/`; tests live in `tests/`.
The pre-commit hook checks formatting, lint, types, and tests without rewriting
your files. GitHub Actions runs the same checks on Python 3.13.

Dependabot checks uv dependencies and GitHub Actions weekly. Husky and pnpm
versions are maintained manually; npm updates are intentionally not enabled.
